{
  "title": "41: Fusselat فصلت",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nحٰمٓ‌ ۚ‏(1)\nHAA-MEEM.\nHa, Meem.\nتَنْزِيْلٌ مِّنَ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ‌ۚ‏(2)\nTANZEELUM MENAR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nA [gradually] sent down [revelation] from the All-beneficent, the All-merciful,\nكِتٰبٌ فُصِّلَتْ اٰيٰتُهٗ قُرْاٰنًا عَرَبِيًّا لِّقَوْمٍ يَّعْلَمُوْنَۙ‏(3)\nKETAABUN FUSSELAT AAYAATOHU QURAANAN A’RABIYYAL LEQAWMIYN YA’LAMOON.\n[this is] a Book whose signs have been elaborated for a people who have knowledge, an Arabic Quran,\nبَشِيْرًا وَّنَذِيْرًا‌ ۚ فَاَعْرَضَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ فَهُمْ لَا يَسْمَعُوْنَ‏(4)\nBASHEERAWN WA NAZEERAA, FA-A’RAZA AKSAROHUM FAHUM LAA YASMA-O’ON.\na bearer of good news and a warner. But most of them turn away [from it], [and] so they do not listen.\nوَقَالُوْا قُلُوْبُنَا فِىْۤ اَكِنَّةٍ مِّمَّا تَدْعُوْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِ وَفِىْۤ اٰذَانِنَا وَقْرٌ وَّمِنْۢ بَيْنِنَا وَبَيْنِكَ حِجَابٌ فَاعْمَلْ اِنَّنَا عٰمِلُوْنَ‏(5)\nWA QAALOO QOLOOBONAA FEE AKINNATIM MIMMAA TAD-O’ONAA EALYHE WA FEE AAZAANENAA WAQRUWN WA MIM BAYNENAA WA BAYNEKA HEJAABUN FA’MAL INNANAA A’AMELOON.\nThey say, ‘Our hearts are in veils [which shut them off] from what you invite us to, and there is a deafness in our ears, and there is a curtain between us and you. So act [as your faith requires]; we too are acting [according to our own].’\nقُلْ اِنَّمَاۤ اَنَا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُكُمْ يُوْحٰٓى اِلَىَّ اَنَّمَاۤ اِلٰهُكُمْ اِلٰهٌ وَّاحِدٌ فَاسْتَقِيْمُوْۤا اِلَيْهِ وَاسْتَغْفِرُوْهُ‌ ؕ وَوَيْلٌ لِّلْمُشْرِكِيْنَ ۙ‏(6)\nQUL INNAMAA ANAA BASHARUM MISLOKUM YOOHAA ELAYYA ANNAMAA ELAAHOKUM ELAAHUWN WAAHEDUN FASTAQEEMOO ELAYHE WAS-TAGHFEROOH, WA WAYLUL LILMUSHREKEENAL.\nSay, ‘I am just a human like you. It has been revealed to me that your God is the One God. So worship Him single-mindedly and plead to Him for forgiveness.’ And woe to the polytheists\nالَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْتُوْنَ الزَّكٰوةَ وَهُمْ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ هُمْ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(7)\nLAZEENA LAA YOATOONAZ ZAKAATA WA HUM BIL AAKHERATE HUM KAAFEROON.\n—those who do not pay the zakat and disbelieve in the Hereafter.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ لَهُمْ اَجْرٌ غَيْرُ مَمْنُوْنٍ‏(8)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE LAHUM AJRUN GHAYRO MAMNOON.\nAs for those who have faith and do righteous deeds, there will be an everlasting reward for them.\nقُلْ اَئِنَّكُمْ لَتَكْفُرُوْنَ بِالَّذِىْ خَلَقَ الْاَرْضَ فِىْ يَوْمَيْنِ وَتَجْعَلُوْنَ لَهٗۤ اَنْدَادًا‌ؕ ذٰلِكَ رَبُّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(9)\nQUL AINNAKUM LATAKFOROONA BIL-LAZEE KHALAQAL ARZA FEE YAWMAYNE WA TAJ-A’LOONA LAHU ANDAADAA, ZAALEKA RABBUL A’ALAMEEN.\nSay, ‘Do you really disbelieve in Him who created the earth in two days, and ascribe partners to Him? That is the Lord of all the worlds!’\nوَجَعَلَ فِيْهَا رَوَاسِىَ مِنْ فَوْقِهَا وَبٰرَكَ فِيْهَا وَقَدَّرَ فِيْهَاۤ اَقْوَاتَهَا فِىْۤ اَرْبَعَةِ اَيَّامٍؕ سَوَآءً لِّلسَّآئِلِيْنَ‏(10)\nWA JA-A’LA FEEHAA AQWAATAHAA FEE ARBA-A’TE AYYAAM, SAWAAA-AL LIS-SAAELEEN.\nHe set in it firm mountains, [rising] above it, blessed it, and ordained in it, in four days, [various] means of sustenance, equally for all seekers.\nثُمَّ اسْتَوٰۤى اِلَى السَّمَآءِ وَهِىَ دُخَانٌ فَقَالَ لَهَا وَلِلْاَرْضِ ائْتِيَا طَوْعًا اَوْ كَرْهًا ؕ قَالَتَاۤ اَتَيْنَا طَآئِعِيْنَ‏(11)\nSUMMAS TAWAA ELAS SAMAAA-E WA HEYA DOKHAANUN FAQAALA LAHAA WA LILARZEA TEYAA TAWA’N AW KARHAA, QAALATAA ATAYNAA TAAA-E-E’EN.\nThen He turned to the heaven, and it was smoke, and He said to it and to the earth, ‘Come, willingly or unwillingly!’ They said, ‘We come obediently.’\nفَقَضٰٮهُنَّ سَبْعَ سَمٰوَاتٍ فِىْ يَوْمَيْنِ وَاَوْحٰى فِىْ كُلِّ سَمَآءٍ اَمْرَهَا‌ ؕ وَزَ يَّنَّا السَّمَآءَ الدُّنْيَا بِمَصَابِيْحَ ‌ۖ  وَحِفْظًا ‌ؕ ذٰ لِكَ تَقْدِيْرُ الْعَزِيْزِ الْعَلِيْمِ‏(12)\nFAQAZAAHUNNA SAB-A’ SAMAAWAATIN FEE YAWMAYNE WA AWHAA FEE KULLE SAMAAA-IN AMRAHAA, WA ZAYYANNAS SAMAAA-AD DUNYAA BEMASAABEEH, WA HIFZAA, ZAALEKA TAQDEERUL A’ZEEZIL A’LEEM.\nThen He set them up as seven heavens in two days, and revealed [to the angels] in each heaven its ordinance. We have adorned the lowest heaven with lamps, and guarded them. That is the ordaining of the All-mighty, the All-knowing.\nفَاِنْ اَعْرَضُوْا فَقُلْ اَنْذَرْتُكُمْ صٰعِقَةً مِّثْلَ صٰعِقَةِ عَادٍ وَّثَمُوْدَ ؕ‏(13)\nFA-IN A-A’RAZOO FAQUL ANZARTOKUM SAA-E’QATAM MISLA SAA-E’QATE A’ADIWN WA SAMOOD.\nBut if they turn away, say, ‘I warn you of a thunderbolt, like the thunderbolt of ‘Ad and Thamud.’\nاِذْ جَآءَتْهُمُ الرُّسُلُ مِنْۢ بَيْنِ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَمِنْ خَلْفِهِمْ اَلَّا تَعْبُدُوْۤا اِلَّا اللّٰهَ‌ؕ قَالُوْا لَوْ شَآءَ رَبُّنَا لَاَنْزَلَ مَلٰٓئِكَةً فَاِنَّا بِمَاۤ اُرْسِلْتُمْ بِهٖ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(14)\nIZ JAAA-ATHOMUR ROSOLO MIM BAYNE AYDEEHIM WA MIN KHALFEHIM ALLAA TA’BODOO ILLAL LAAH, QAALOO LAW SHAAA-A RABBONAA LA-ANZALA MALAAA-EKATAN FAINNAA BEMAA URSILTUM BEHI KAAFEROON.\nWhen the apostles came to them, before them and in their own time, saying, ‘Worship no one except Allah!’ They said, ‘Had our Lord wished, He would have sent down angels [to us]. We indeed disbelieve in what you have been sent with.’\nفَاَمَّا عَادٌ فَاسْتَكْبَرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ وَقَالُوْا مَنْ اَشَدُّ مِنَّا قُوَّةً  ‌ؕ اَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَهُمْ هُوَ اَشَدُّ مِنْهُمْ قُوَّةً  ؕ وَكَانُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا يَجْحَدُوْنَ‏(15)\nFA-AMMAA A’ADUN FASTAKBAROO FIL ARZE BEGHAYRIL HAQQE WA QAALOO MAN ASHADDO MINNAA QUWWAH, AWA LAM YARAW ANNAL LAAHAL LAZEE KHALAQAHUM HOWA ASHADDO MINHUM QUWWAH, WA KAANOO BEAAYAATENAA YAJHADOON.\nAs for [the people of] ‘Ad, they acted arrogantly in the earth unduly, and they said, ‘Who is more powerful than us?’ Did they not see that Allah, who created them, is more powerful than them? They used to impugn Our signs;\nفَاَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ رِيْحًا صَرْصَرًا فِىْۤ اَيَّامٍ نَّحِسَاتٍ لِّنُذِيْقَهُمْ عَذَابَ الْخِزْىِ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا‌ ؕ وَلَعَذَابُ الْاٰخِرَةِ اَخْزٰى‌ وَهُمْ لَا يُنْصَرُوْنَ‏(16)\nFA-ARSALNAA A’LAYHIM REEHAN SARSARAN FEE AYYAAMIN NAHESAATIL LENOZEEQAHUM A’ZAABAL KHIZYE FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA, WA LA-A’ZAABUL AAKHERATE AKHZAA WA HUM LAA YUNSAROON.\nso We unleashed upon them an icy gale during ill-fated days, in order that We might make them taste a humiliating punishment in the life of the world. Yet the punishment of the Hereafter will be surely more disgraceful, and they will not be helped.\nوَاَمَّا ثَمُوْدُ فَهَدَيْنٰهُمْ فَاسْتَحَبُّوا الْعَمٰى عَلَى الْهُدٰى فَاَخَذَتْهُمْ صٰعِقَةُ الْعَذَابِ الْهُوْنِ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(17)\nWA AMMAA SAMOODO FAHADAYNAAHUM FASTAHABBUL A’MAA A’LAL HODAA FA-AKHAZATHUM SAA-E’QATUL A’ZAABIL HOONE BEMAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nAs for [the people of] Thamud, We guided them, but they preferred blindness to guidance. So the bolt of a humiliating punishment seized them because of what they used to earn.\nوَ نَجَّيْنَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَكَانُوْا يَتَّقُوْنَ‏(18)\nWA NAJJAYNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA KAANU YATTAQOON.\nAnd We delivered those who had faith and were Godwary.\nوَيَوْمَ يُحْشَرُ اَعْدَآءُ اللّٰهِ اِلَى النَّارِ فَهُمْ يُوْزَعُوْنَ‏(19)\nWA YAWMA YOHSHARO A-A’DAAA-UL LAAHE ELAN NAARE FAHUM YOOZA-O’ON.\nThe day the enemies of Allah are marched out toward the Fire, while they are in check,\nحَتّٰٓى اِذَا مَا جَآءُوْهَا شَهِدَ عَلَيْهِمْ سَمْعُهُمْ وَاَبْصَارُهُمْ وَجُلُوْدُهُمْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(20)\nHATTAA IZAA MAA JAAA-OOHAA SHAHEDA A’LAYHIM SAM-O’HUM WA ABSAAROHUM WA JOLOODOHUM BEMAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nwhen they come to it, their hearing, their eyes and their skins will bear witness against them concerning what they used to do.\nوَقَالُوْا لِجُلُوْدِهِمْ لِمَ شَهِدْتُّمْ عَلَيْنَا‌ ؕ قَالُوْۤا اَنْطَقَنَا اللّٰهُ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْطَقَ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ وَّهُوَ خَلَقَكُمْ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ وَّاِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(21)\nWA QAALOO LEJOLOODEHIM LEMA SHAHIT-TUM A’LAYNAA, QAALOO ANTAQANAL LAAHUL LAZEE ANTAQA KULLA SHAY-IWN WA HOWA KHALAQAKUM AWWALA MARRATIWN WA ELAYHE TURJA-O’ON.\nThey will say to their skins, ‘Why did you bear witness against us?’ They will say, ‘We were given speech by Allah, who gave speech to all things. He created you the first time, and you are being brought back to Him.\nوَمَا كُنْتُمْ تَسْتَتِرُوْنَ اَنْ يَّشْهَدَ عَلَيْكُمْ سَمْعُكُمْ وَلَاۤ اَبْصَارُكُمْ وَلَا جُلُوْدُكُمْ وَلٰكِنْ ظَنَنْتُمْ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَعْلَمُ كَثِيْرًا مِّمَّا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(22)\nWA MAA KUNTUM TASTATEROONA AYN YASHHADA A’LAYKUM SAM-O’KUM WA LAA ABSAAROKUM WA LAA JOLOODOKUM WA LAAKIN ZANANTUM ANNAL LAAHA LAA YA’LAMO KASEERAM MIMMA TA’MALOON.\nYou did not use to conceal yourselves [while perpetrating sinful acts] lest your hearing, your eyes, or your skins should bear witness against you, but you thought that Allah did not know most of what you did.\nوَذٰلِكُمْ ظَنُّكُمُ الَّذِىْ ظَنَنْتُمْ بِرَبِّكُمْ اَرْدٰٮكُمْ فَاَصْبَحْتُمْ مِّنَ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ‏(23)\nWA ZAALEKUM ZANNOKOMUL LAZEE ZANANTUM BERABBEKUM ARDAAKUM FA-ASBAHTUM MENAL KHAASEREEN.\nThat misjudgement, which you entertained about your Lord ruined you. So you became losers.’\nفَاِنْ يَّصْبِرُوْا فَالنَّارُ مَثْوًى لَّهُمْ‌ؕ وَاِنْ يَّسْتَعْتِبُوْا فَمَا هُمْ مِّنَ الْمُعْتَبِيْنَ‏(24)\nFAIYN YASBEROO FANNAARO MASWAL LAHUM, WA IYN YASTA’TEBOO FAMAA HUM MENAL MOA’TABEEN.\nShould they be patient, the Fire is their abode; and should they seek to propitiate [Allah], they will not be redeemed.\nوَقَيَّضْنَا لَهُمْ قُرَنَآءَ فَزَيَّنُوْا لَهُمْ مَّا بَيْنَ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَمَا خَلْفَهُمْ وَحَقَّ عَلَيْهِمُ الْقَوْلُ فِىْۤ اُمَمٍ قَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ مِّنَ الْجِنِّ وَالْاِنْسِ‌ۚ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا خٰسِرِيْنَ‏(25)\nWA QAYYAZNAA LAHUM QORANAAA-A FA-ZAYYANOO LAHUM MAA BAYNA AYDEEHIM WA MAA KHALFAHUM WA HAQQA A’LAYHEMUL QAWLO FEE OMAMIN QAD KHALAT MIN QABLEHIM MENAL JINNE WAL-INS, INNAHUM KAANOO KHAASEREEN.\nWe have assigned them companions who make their present [conduct] and future [state] seem decorous to them, and the word became due against them along with the nations of jinn and humans that passed away before them. They were indeed losers.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَا تَسْمَعُوْا لِهٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنِ وَالْغَوْا فِيْهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَغْلِبُوْنَ‏(26)\nWA QAALAL LAZEENA KAFAROO LAA TASMA-O’O LEHAAZAL QUR-AANE WAL GHAW FEEHE LA-A’LLAKUM TAGHLEBOON.\nThe faithless say, ‘Do not listen to this Quran and hoot it down so that you may prevail [over the Apostle].’\nفَلَنُذِيْقَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا عَذَابًا شَدِيْدًاۙ وَّلَنَجْزِيَنَّهُمْ اَسْوَاَ الَّذِىْ كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(27)\nFALANOZEEQANNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO A’ZAABAN SHADEEDAWN WA LANAJZEYANNAHUM ASWA-AL LAZEE KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nWe will surely make the faithless taste a severe punishment, and We will surely requite them by the worst of what they used to do.\nذٰ لِكَ جَزَآءُ اَعْدَآءِ اللّٰهِ النَّارُ‌ ۚ لَهُمْ فِيْهَا دَارُ الْخُلْدِ‌ ؕ جَزَآءًۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا يَجْحَدُوْنَ‏(28)\nZAALEKA JAZAAA-O A-A’DAAA-IL LAAHIN NAAR, LAHUM FEEHAA DAARUL KHULD, JAZAAA-AM BEMAA KAANOO BE-AAYAATENAA YAJHADOON.\nThat is the requital of the enemies of Allah—the Fire! In it, they will have an everlasting abode, as a requital for their impugning Our signs.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا رَبَّنَاۤ اَرِنَا الَّذَيْنِ اَضَلّٰنَا مِنَ الْجِنِّ وَالْاِنْسِ نَجْعَلْهُمَا تَحْتَ اَقْدَامِنَا لِيَكُوْنَا مِنَ الْاَسْفَلِيْنَ‏(29)\nWA QAALAL LAZEENA KAFAROO RABBANAA ARENAL LAZEENA AZALLAANAA MENAL JINNE WAL INSE NAJ-A’LHOMAA TAHTA AQDAAMENAA LEYAKOONA MENAL ASFALEEN.\nThe faithless will say, ‘Our Lord! Show us those who led us astray from among jinn and humans so that we may trample them under our feet, so that they may be among the lowermost!’\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ قَالُوْا رَبُّنَا اللّٰهُ ثُمَّ اسْتَقَامُوْا تَتَنَزَّلُ عَلَيْهِمُ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ اَلَّا تَخَافُوْا وَلَا تَحْزَنُوْا وَاَبْشِرُوْا بِالْجَنَّةِ الَّتِىْ كُنْتُمْ تُوْعَدُوْنَ‏(30)\nINNAL LAZEENA QAALOO RABBONAL LAAHO SUMMAS-TAQAAMOO TATANAZZALO A’LAYHEMUL MALAAA-EKATO ALLAA TAKHAAFOO WA LAA TAHZANOO WA ABSHEROO BIL-JANNATIL LATEE KUNTUM TOO-A’DOON.\nIndeed those who say, ‘Our Lord is Allah!’ and then remain steadfast, the angels descend upon them, [saying,] ‘Do not fear, nor be grieved! Receive the good news of the paradise, which you have been promised.\nنَحْنُ اَوْلِيٰٓؤُکُمْ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَفِى الْاٰخِرَةِ ۚ وَلَكُمْ فِيْهَا مَا تَشْتَهِىْۤ اَنْفُسُكُمْ وَلَكُمْ فِيْهَا مَا تَدَّعُوْنَ ؕ‏(31)\nNAHNO AWLEYAAA-OKUM FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA WA FIL AAKHERAH, WA LAKUM FEEHAA MAA TASHTAHEE ANFOSOKUM WA LAKUM FEEHAA MAA TADDA-O’ON.\nWe are your friends in the life of this world and in the Hereafter, and you will have in it whatever your souls desire, and you will have in it whatever you ask for,\nنُزُلًا مِّنْ غَفُوْرٍ رَّحِيْمٍ‏(32)\nNOZOLAM MIN GHAFOORIR RAHEEM.\nas a hospitality from One all-forgiving, all-merciful.’\nوَمَنْ اَحْسَنُ قَوْلًا مِّمَّنْ دَعَاۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا وَّقَالَ اِنَّنِىْ مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(33)\nWA MAN AHSANO QAWLAM MIMMAA DA-A’A ELAL LAAHE WA A’MELA SAALEHAWN WA QAALA INNANEE MENAL MUSLEMEEN.\nWho has a better call than him who summons to Allah and acts righteously and says, ‘Indeed I am one of the Muslims’?\nوَلَا تَسْتَوِى الْحَسَنَةُ وَ لَا السَّيِّئَةُ ؕ اِدْفَعْ بِالَّتِىْ هِىَ اَحْسَنُ فَاِذَا الَّذِىْ بَيْنَكَ وَبَيْنَهٗ عَدَاوَةٌ كَاَنَّهٗ وَلِىٌّ حَمِيْمٌ‏(34)\nWA LAA TASTAWIL HASANATO WA LASSAYYEAH, IDFA’ BILLATEE HEYA AHSANO FA-IZAL LAZEE BAYNAKA WA BAYNAHU A’DAAWATUN KA-ANNAHU WALIYYUN HAMEEM.\nGood and evil [conduct] are not equal. Repel [evil] with what is best. [If you do so,] he between whom and you was enmity, will then be as though he were a sympathetic friend.\nوَمَا يُلَقّٰٮهَاۤ اِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ صَبَرُوْا‌ۚ وَمَا يُلَقّٰٮهَاۤ اِلَّا ذُوْ حَظٍّ عَظِيْمٍ‏(35)\nWA MAA YOLAQQAAHAA ILLAL LAZEENA SABAROO, WA MAA YOLAQQAAHAA ILLAA ZOO HAZZIN A’ZEEM.\nBut none is granted it except those who are patient, and none is granted it except the greatly endowed.\nوَاِمَّا يَنْزَغَنَّكَ مِنَ الشَّيْطٰنِ نَزْغٌ فَاسْتَعِذْ بِاللّٰهِ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(36)\nWA AMMAA YANZAGHANNAKA MENASH SHAYTAANE NAZGHUN FAS-TA-I’Z BILLAAH, INNAHU HOWAS SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nShould an incitement from Satan prompt you [to ill feeling], seek the protection of Allah. Indeed, He is the All-hearing, the All-knowing.\nوَمِنْ اٰيٰتِهِ الَّيْلُ وَالنَّهَارُ وَالشَّمْسُ وَالْقَمَرُ‌ؕ لَا تَسْجُدُوْا لِلشَّمْسِ وَلَا لِلْقَمَرِ وَاسْجُدُوْا لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَهُنَّ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ اِيَّاهُ تَعْبُدُوْنَ‏(37)\nWA MIN AAYAATEHIL LAYLO WAN NAHAARO????\nAmong His signs are night and day, and the sun and the moon. Do not prostrate to the sun, nor to the moon, but prostrate to Allah who created them, if it is Him that you worship.\nفَاِنِ اسْتَكْبَرُوْا فَالَّذِيْنَ عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ يُسَبِّحُوْنَ لَهٗ بِالَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ وَهُمْ لَا يَسْئَمُوْنَ۩‏(38)\n38:\nBut if they disdain [the worship of Allah], those who are near your Lord glorify Him night and day, and they are not wearied.\nوَمِنْ اٰيٰتِهٖۤ اَنَّكَ تَرَى الْاَرْضَ خَاشِعَةً فَاِذَاۤ اَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْهَا الْمَآءَ اهْتَزَّتْ وَرَبَتْ‌ؕ اِنَّ الَّذِىْۤ اَحْيَاهَا لَمُحْىِ الْمَوْتٰى ؕ اِنَّهٗ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(39)\nWA MIN AAYAATEHI ANNAKA TARAL ARZA KHAASHEA’TAN FA-EZAA ANZALNAA A’LAYHAL MAAA-AH TAZZAT WA RABAT, INNAL LAZEE AHYAAHAA LAMOHYIL MAWTAA, INNAHU A’LAA KULLE SHAYIN QADEER.\nAmong His signs, is that you see the earth desolate; but when We send down water upon it, it stirs and swells. Indeed, He who revives it will also revive the dead. Indeed, He has power over all things.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يُلْحِدُوْنَ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِنَا لَا يَخْفَوْنَ عَلَيْنَا ؕ اَفَمَنْ يُّلْقٰى فِى النَّارِ خَيْرٌ اَمْ مَّنْ يَّاْتِىْۤ اٰمِنًا يَّوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ‌ ؕ اِعْمَلُوْا مَا شِئْتُمْ‌ ۙ اِنَّهٗ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ بَصِيْرٌ‏(40)\nINNAL LAZEENA YULHEDOONA FEE AAYAATENAA LAA YAKHFAWNA A’LAYNAA, AFAMAYN YULQAA FIN NAARE KHAYRUN AM MAYN YAATEE AAMENAYN YAWMAL QEYAAMAH, EA’MALOO MAA SHEATUM, INNAHU BEMAA TA’MALOONA BASEER.\nThose who abuse Our signs are not hidden from Us. Is someone who is cast in the Fire better off, or someone who arrives safely on the Day of Resurrection? Act as you wish; indeed He watches what you do.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِالذِّكْرِ لَمَّا جَآءَهُمْ‌ۚ وَاِنَّهٗ لَكِتٰبٌ عَزِيْزٌۙ‏(41)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO BIZ-ZIKRE LAMMAA JAAA-AHUM, WA INNAHU LAKETAABUN A’ZEEZUL.\nThose who reject the Reminder when it comes to them... Indeed, it is an august Book:\nلَّا يَاْتِيْهِ الْبَاطِلُ مِنْۢ بَيْنِ يَدَيْهِ وَلَا مِنْ خَلْفِهٖ‌ؕ تَنْزِيْلٌ مِّنْ حَكِيْمٍ حَمِيْدٍ‏(42)\nLAA YAATEEHIL BAATELO MIM BAYNE YADAYHE WA LAA MIN KHALFEH, TANZEELUM MIN HAKEEMIN HAMEED.\nfalsehood cannot approach it, at present or in future, a [revelation gradually] sent down from One all-wise, all-laudable.\nمَا يُقَالُ لَكَ اِلَّا مَا قَدْ قِيْلَ لِلرُّسُلِ مِنْ قَبْلِكَ ‌ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَذُوْ مَغْفِرَةٍ وَّذُوْ عِقَابٍ اَ لِيْمٍ‏(43)\nMAA YOQAALO LAKA ILLAA MAA QAD QEELA LIR-ROSOLE MIN QABLEK, INNA RABBEKA LA-ZOO MAGHFERATIWN WA ZOO E’QAABIN ALEEM.\nNothing is said to you except what has already been said to the apostles before you. Indeed your Lord is One who forgives and also metes out a painful retribution.\nوَلَوْ جَعَلْنٰهُ قُرْاٰنًا اَعْجَمِيًّا لَّقَالُوْا لَوْلَا فُصِّلَتْ اٰيٰتُهٗ ؕ ءَؔاَعْجَمِىٌّ وَّعَرَبِىٌّ‌  ؕ قُلْ هُوَ لِلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا هُدًى وَشِفَآءٌ‌  ؕ وَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ فِىْۤ اٰذَانِهِمْ وَقْرٌ وَّهُوَ عَلَيْهِمْ عَمًى‌ ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ يُنَادَوْنَ مِنْ مَّكَانٍۢ بَعِيْدٍ‏(44)\nWA LAW JA-A’LNAAHO QURAANAN A-A’JAMIYYAL LAQAALOO LAWLAA FUSSELAT AAYAATOH, A-AA’JAMIYYUWN WA A’RABEE, QUL HOWA LILLAZEENA AAMANOO HODAWN WA SHEFAAA, WAL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA FEE AAZAANEHIM WAQRUWN WA HOWA A’LAYHIM A’MA, OOLAAA-EKA YONAADAWNA MIM MAKAANIM BA-E’ED.\nHad We made it a non-Arabic Quran, they would have said, ‘Why have not its signs been articulated?’ ‘What! A non-Arabian [scripture] and an Arabian [prophet]!?’ Say, ‘It is guidance and healing for those who have faith. As for those who are faithless, there is a deafness in their ears and it is lost to their sight: [to them it is as if] they were called from a distant place.’\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ فَاخْتُلِفَ فِيْهِ‌ؕ وَلَوْلَا كَلِمَةٌ سَبَقَتْ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ لَقُضِىَ بَيْنَهُمْ‌ؕ وَاِنَّهُمْ لَفِىْ شَكٍّ مِّنْهُ مُرِيْبٍ‏(45)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA FAKHTOLEFA FEEH, WA LAWLAA KALEMATUN SABAQAT MIR RABBEKA LAQOZEYA BAYNAHUM, WA INNAHUM LAFEE SHAKKIM MINHO MOREEB.\nCertainly We gave Moses the Book, but differences arose about it; and were it not for a prior decree of your Lord, judgement would have been made between them, for they are in grave doubt concerning it.\nمَنْ عَمِلَ صَالِحًا فَلِنَفْسِهٖ‌ وَمَنْ اَسَآءَ فَعَلَيْهَا‌ؕ وَمَا رَبُّكَ بِظَلَّامٍ لِّلْعَبِيْدِ‏(46)\nMAN A’MELA SAALEHAN FALENAFSEH, WA MAN ASAAA-A FA-A’LAYHAA, WA MAA RABBOKA BEZALLAAMIL LIL-A’BEED.\nWhoever acts righteously, it is for [the benefit of] his own soul, and whoever does evil, it is to its detriment, and your Lord is not tyrannical to His servants.\nاِلَيْهِ يُرَدُّ عِلْمُ السَّاعَةِ‌ؕ وَمَا تَخْرُجُ مِنْ ثَمَرٰتٍ مِّنْ اَكْمَامِهَا وَمَا تَحْمِلُ مِنْ اُنْثٰى وَلَا تَضَعُ اِلَّا بِعِلْمِهٖ‌ؕ وَيَوْمَ يُنَادِيْهِمْ اَيْنَ شُرَكَآءِىْۙ قَالُوْۤا اٰذَنّٰكَۙ مَا مِنَّا مِنْ شَهِيْدٍ‌ۚ‏(47)\nELAYHE YORADDO I’LMUS SAA-A’H, WA MAA TAKHROJO MIN SAMARAATIM MIN AKMAAMEHAA WA MAA TAHMELO MIN UNSAA WA LAA TAZAA-O’ ILLAA BE-I’LMEH, WA YAWMA YONAADEEHIM AYNA SHORAKAAA-EE, QAALOO AAZANNAKA MAA MINNAA MIN SHAHEED.\nOn Him devolves the knowledge of the Hour, and no fruit emerges from its covering and no female conceives or delivers except with His knowledge. On the day when He will call out to them, ‘Where are My ‘partners’?’ They will say, ‘We informed You that there is no witness amongst us.’\nوَضَلَّ عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ قَبْلُ‌ وَظَنُّوْا مَا لَهُمْ مِّنْ مَّحِيْصٍ‏(48)\nWA ZALLA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YADOONA MIN QABLO WA ZANNOO MAA LAHUM MIM MAHEES.\nWhat they used to invoke before has forsaken them, and they know there is no escape for them.\nلَا يَسْئَمُ الْاِنْسَانُ مِنْ دُعَآءِ الْخَيْرِ وَاِنْ مَّسَّهُ الشَّرُّ فَيَئُوْسٌ قَنُوْطٌ‏(49)\nLAA YAS-AMUL INSAANO MIN DO-A’AA-IL KHAYR, WA IM MASSAHUSH SHARRO FAYAOOSUN QANOOT.\nMan is never wearied of supplicating for good, and should any ill befall him, he becomes hopeless and despondent.\nوَلَئِنْ اَذَقْنٰهُ رَحْمَةً مِّنَّا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ ضَرَّآءَ مَسَّتْهُ لَيَقُوْلَنَّ هٰذَا لِىْ ۙ وَمَاۤ اَظُنُّ السَّاعَةَ قَآئِمَةً  ۙ وَّلَئِنْ رُّجِعْتُ اِلٰى رَبِّىْۤ اِنَّ لِىْ عِنْدَهٗ لَلْحُسْنٰى‌ ۚ فَلَنُنَبِّئَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِمَا عَمِلُوْا وَلَنُذِيْقَنَّهُمْ مِّنْ عَذَابٍ غَلِيْظٍ‏(50)\nWA LA-IN AZAQNAAHO RAHMATAM MINNAA MIM BA’DE ZARAAA-A MASSATHO LAYAQOOLANNA HAAZAA LEE, WA MAA AZUNNUS SAA-A’TA QAAA-EMATAWN, WA LA-IR ROJE’TO ELAA RABBEE INNA LEE I’NDAHU LAL-HUSNAA, FALANONABBE-ANNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO BEMAA A’MELOO, WA LANOZEEQANNAHUM MIN A’ZAABIN GHALEEZ.\nIf, after distress has befallen him, We let him have a taste of Our mercy, he says, ‘This is my due! I do not think the Hour will ever come, and in case I am returned to my Lord, I will indeed have the best [reward] with Him.’ So We will surely inform the faithless about what they have done, and will surely make them taste a harsh punishment.\nوَاِذَاۤ اَنْعَمْنَا عَلَى الْاِنْسَانِ اَعْرَضَ وَنَاٰ بِجَانِبِهٖ‌ۚ وَاِذَا مَسَّهُ الشَّرُّ فَذُوْ دُعَآءٍ عَرِيْضٍ‏(51)\nWA EZAA AN-A’MNAA A’LAL INSAANE A-A’RAZA WA NA-AA BEJAANEBEH, WA EZAA MASSAHUSH SHARRO FAZOO DO-A’AA-IN A’REEZ.\nWhen We bless man, he is disregardful and turns aside; but when an ill befalls him, he makes protracted supplications.\nقُلْ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ كَانَ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِ ثُمَّ كَفَرْتُمْ بِهٖ مَنْ اَضَلُّ مِمَّنْ هُوَ فِىْ شِقَاقٍۢ بَعِيْدٍ‏(52)\nQUL ARA-AYTUM IN KAANA MIN I’NDIL LAAHE SUMMA KAFARTUM BEHI MAN AZALLO MIMMAN HOWA FEE SHEQAAQIM BA-E’ED.\nSay, ‘Tell me, if it is from Allah and you disbelieve in it, who will be more astray than those who are in extreme defiance.’\nسَنُرِيْهِمْ اٰيٰتِنَا فِى الْاٰفَاقِ وَفِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ حَتّٰى يَتَبَيَّنَ لَهُمْ اَنَّهُ الْحَقُّ‌ ؕ اَوَلَمْ يَكْفِ بِرَبِّكَ اَنَّهٗ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ شَهِيْدٌ‏(53)\nSANOREEHIM AAYAATENAA FIL AAFAAQE WA FEE ANFOSEHIM HATTAA YATABAYYANA LAHUM ANNAHUL HAQ, AWA LAM YAKFE BERABBEKA ANNAHU A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN SHAHEED.\nSoon We shall show them Our signs in the horizons and in their own souls until it becomes clear to them that He is the Real. Is it not sufficient that your Lord is witness to all things?\nاَلَاۤ اِنَّهُمْ فِىْ مِرْيَةٍ مِّنْ لِّقَآءِ رَبِّهِمْ‌ؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّهٗ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ مُّحِيْطٌ‏(54)\nALAA INNAHUM FEE MIRYATIM MIL LEQAAA-E RABBEHIM, ALAA INNAHU BEKULLE SHAY-IM MOHEET.\nIndeed, they are in doubt about the encounter with their Lord! Indeed, He embraces all things!",
  "merits": "Surah Haameem Sajdah\nAnother name for this Surah is Fusselat. This is a ‘Makki’ Surah that has 54 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that for each letter of this Surah that is recited, ten rewards are given.\nIt is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that the one who recites Surah Haameem Sajdah will have light shining on front of him on the Day of Judgement and his life in this world will be praiseworthy. If this Surah is written in a container and rainwater is then collected in it and put on one’s eyes, then it alleviates all eye problems."
